# Bulk regression case (assistant-written): the three declarations that need a
# body and do not have one. Each is reported at the NEXT declaration's line —
# except the last, which has no next declaration in this file and falls back to
# its own keyword. It used to point at the EOF line; the library appended to
# every compilation (§1.11) made that "the library's first line", which is a
# place the author cannot open, so `Cursor::here_or` clamps it here instead.
#
# **Corrected 2026-09-13 (M-handle-verdict step 4): `empty_record` is no longer
# one of them.** It landed on the next declaration's line for the same reason
# the others do — by the time it fires, the parser has crossed the record's own
# line end — and that made it underline a line the author had done nothing wrong
# on. It now underlines `record <Name>`, which is the text to change, so its
# annotation moved up two lines. The other two are unchanged and the sentence
# above still describes them.
constant MAX: i64

record Point  #~ missing_body #~ empty_record

variant Token  #~ empty_variant
